<Layout title="Experience" description="Professional experience spanning DC CAP, Common App, University of Virginia, and Teach For America. PhD, MPP, IES Fellow.">
	<div class="mx-auto max-w-5xl px-6 py-16 lg:px-8 lg:py-24">
		<h1 class="text-h1 mb-6 font-semibold text-neutral-900">
			Experience
		</h1>

		<p class="text-dek mb-16 max-w-3xl font-heading text-neutral-900">
			Across classrooms, academic research, the largest college application dataset in the country, and nonprofit leadership, I've built the teams and the systems that move outcomes for students.
		</p>

		<div class="space-y-20">
			<section>
				<h2 class="text-h2 mb-12 font-semibold text-neutral-900">
					Professional Experience
				</h2>

				<div class="space-y-16 border-l-2 border-neutral-200 pl-16 sm:pl-28">
					<div class="relative">
						<div
							class="absolute -left-[11px] top-2 h-3 w-3 rounded-full border-2 border-white bg-primary"
						></div>
						<div class="pl-6">
							<h3 class="text-h3 font-semibold text-neutral-900">
								Chief Strategy and Analytics Officer | DC CAP
							</h3>
							<p class="mt-1 text-base text-neutral-600">July 2023 – Present | Washington, DC</p>

							<div class="mt-6 space-y-4 text-base leading-relaxed text-neutral-700">
								<p>
									<strong class="font-semibold text-neutral-900">Executive Leadership:</strong> I serve on the Senior Leadership Team, reporting to the CEO, and help lead DC CAP toward its <a href="https://www.dccap.org/blog/dccap-announces-2050-moonshot-goal" class="text-primary underline underline-offset-2 hover:text-primary/80">2050 Moonshot</a> of 80% college completion for DC students. I lead five units, Student Success, University Partnerships, GEAR UP, Innovation, and Data & Technology, along with the financial planning and analysis function. I have five direct reports, including the Chief Programs Officer, and give strategic direction to managers across the organization.
								</p>

								<p>
									<strong class="font-semibold text-neutral-900">Strategy:</strong> When I arrived, I ran a full evaluation of our university partnerships, and the findings drove our pivot to a regional partnership model, now Pillar 1 of the FY26–28 strategy. We exited five underperforming partners, brought on new ones, and rewrote our partner agreements around retention. DC CAP retained scholars at <strong class="font-semibold text-neutral-900">90%, 85%, and 88%</strong> over the past three years, and <strong class="font-semibold text-neutral-900">76%</strong> of Class of 2021 scholars in our flagship University Partnership program earned a degree within five years, with partner campuses ranging from 57% to 100%. The full year is public in our <a href="https://impact.dccap.org/" class="text-primary underline underline-offset-2 hover:text-primary/80">FY26 Impact Report</a>.
								</p>

								<p>
									<strong class="font-semibold text-neutral-900">People and Culture:</strong> I brought four teams together into one Student Success division and built the OKRs it runs on. We cut coach administrative work from about <strong class="font-semibold text-neutral-900">60%</strong> of a coach's time to under 10%, and coaches put that time into a rebuilt professional development model and new strategic work. Across my time at Common App and DC CAP, <strong class="font-semibold text-neutral-900">three</strong> direct reports have earned promotions, one of them twice. I wrote <strong class="font-semibold text-neutral-900">four</strong> Standards of Practice so our institutional knowledge no longer lives in any one person's head.
								</p>

								<p>
									<strong class="font-semibold text-neutral-900">Change Management:</strong> I lead DC CAP's digital transformation. I designed the processes that run the scholar lifecycle, which our team then implemented in Salesforce, and the application process now runs at one person and <strong class="font-semibold text-neutral-900">3–5 hours</strong> a week, down from roughly ten people at 20-plus hours. I designed the AI Governance Framework, ran the 60-day pilot that introduced it to nine staff across three units, and led the leadership AI training, where all nine leaders who completed it improved on DC CAP's own fluency assessment.
								</p>

								<p>
									<strong class="font-semibold text-neutral-900">Innovation + Fundraising:</strong> I launched DC CAP's Innovation Hub on a <strong class="font-semibold text-neutral-900">$600K</strong> KPMG <a href="https://kpmg.com/us/en/media/news/ai-impact-grant-2025.html" class="text-primary underline underline-offset-2 hover:text-primary/80">AI Impact Initiative</a> grant, the organization's largest AI investment to date, and I have been instrumental in more than <strong class="font-semibold text-neutral-900">$50M</strong> in philanthropic commitments since joining. The Hub houses the <a href="https://dccapinnovation.org/" class="text-primary underline underline-offset-2 hover:text-primary/80">AI Governance Framework</a> and the Career Pathway Intelligence Platform, whose first product, the College Navigator, launches October 15, 2026. I built the <a href="https://dccapinnovation.org/data_insights/evidence_room.html" class="text-primary underline underline-offset-2 hover:text-primary/80">DC Evidence Room</a>, a public test of whether college pays off for D.C. students and why the answer varies by place, and I build agentic AI workflows that support our analytics, engineering, web publishing, and grant research and writing.
								</p>

							</div>
						</div>
					</div>

					<div class="relative">
						<div
							class="absolute -left-[11px] top-2 h-3 w-3 rounded-full border-2 border-white bg-primary"
						></div>
						<div class="pl-6">
							<h3 class="text-h3 font-semibold text-neutral-900">
								Senior Manager of Research & Analytics | Common App
							</h3>
							<p class="mt-1 text-base text-neutral-600">Oct 2020 – July 2023 | Remote</p>

							<div class="mt-6 space-y-4 text-base leading-relaxed text-neutral-700">
								<p>
									<strong class="font-semibold text-neutral-900">Founding Team Member:</strong> Second member of the founding research function at Common App, the largest college application dataset in the United States. Defined the data environment, technical stack, research agenda, and data sharing policies, and co-authored the <a href="https://www.commonapp.org/about/reports-and-insights" class="text-primary underline underline-offset-2 hover:text-primary/80">research briefs</a> on <a href="https://commonapp.org/files/Common-App-Brief-Test-Optional-College-Admissions.pdf" class="text-primary underline underline-offset-2 hover:text-primary/80">test-optional admissions</a>, <a href="https://commonapp.org/files/Common-App-Brief-Pandemic-Patterns-First-Year-Applicants.pdf" class="text-primary underline underline-offset-2 hover:text-primary/80">pandemic application patterns</a>, and <a href="https://www.commonapp.org/files/common-app-report-early-admission-student-trends.pdf" class="text-primary underline underline-offset-2 hover:text-primary/80">early admission</a>.
								</p>

								<p>
									<strong class="font-semibold text-neutral-900">External Relations:</strong> Primary spokesperson for data insights, representing the organization to the Board of Directors and to national media, including <a href="https://www.cnbc.com/2021/12/07/college-admission-applications-spike-as-january-deadline-nears.html" class="text-primary underline underline-offset-2 hover:text-primary/80">CNBC</a>, <a href="https://www.marketplace.org/story/2022/08/15/automatic-college-admissions-can-be-a-boon-to-students-and-schools-alike" class="text-primary underline underline-offset-2 hover:text-primary/80">NPR Marketplace</a>, <a href="https://www.insidehighered.com/admissions/article/2021/09/13/study-reveals-which-applicants-didnt-submit-test-scores" class="text-primary underline underline-offset-2 hover:text-primary/80">Inside Higher Ed</a>, and <a href="https://www.highereddive.com/news/what-happened-when-the-common-app-offered-college-students-proactive-admiss/629356/" class="text-primary underline underline-offset-2 hover:text-primary/80">Higher Ed Dive</a>.
								</p>

								<p>
									<strong class="font-semibold text-neutral-900">Strategic Partnerships:</strong> Negotiated and managed research collaborations and data-sharing protocols with leading universities. The resulting work appeared as an <a href="https://www.nber.org/papers/w34260" class="text-primary underline underline-offset-2 hover:text-primary/80">NBER working paper</a> on test-optional admissions, a <a href="https://www.brookings.edu/articles/complex-applications-create-barriers-to-college-some-are-trying-to-change-that/" class="text-primary underline underline-offset-2 hover:text-primary/80">Brookings article</a> on direct admissions, and an <a href="https://edworkingpapers.com/ai23-819" class="text-primary underline underline-offset-2 hover:text-primary/80">EdWorkingPaper</a> from Brown University's Annenberg Institute, and was presented at the Association for Education Finance and Policy (AEFP). I also led Common App's side of a randomized trial of direct admissions, which <a href="https://www.highereddive.com/news/what-happened-when-the-common-app-offered-college-students-proactive-admiss/629356/" class="text-primary underline underline-offset-2 hover:text-primary/80">Higher Ed Dive</a> and <a href="https://www.marketplace.org/story/2022/08/15/automatic-college-admissions-can-be-a-boon-to-students-and-schools-alike" class="text-primary underline underline-offset-2 hover:text-primary/80">Marketplace</a> covered.
								</p>

							</div>
						</div>
					</div>

					<div class="relative">
						<div
							class="absolute -left-[11px] top-2 h-3 w-3 rounded-full border-2 border-white bg-primary"
						></div>
						<div class="pl-6">
							<h3 class="text-h3 font-semibold text-neutral-900">
								IES Predoctoral Fellow, Educational Policy Studies | University of Virginia
							</h3>
							<p class="mt-1 text-base text-neutral-600">Aug 2015 – Aug 2020 | Charlottesville, VA</p>

							<div class="mt-6 space-y-4 text-base leading-relaxed text-neutral-700">
								<p>
									<strong class="font-semibold text-neutral-900">UVA–Louisiana Department of Education Partnership:</strong> Policy and accountability systems research with the Louisiana Department of Education during a multi-year statewide policy rollout (2017–2020). Worked directly with state policymakers and district leaders on accountability design.
								</p>

								<p>
									<strong class="font-semibold text-neutral-900">Published Research:</strong> The partnership produced peer-reviewed research on statewide policy implementation and program quality. Our study of systemwide quality improvement under Louisiana's rating system appeared in <a href="https://journals.sagepub.com/doi/10.1177/23328584211011610" class="text-primary underline underline-offset-2 hover:text-primary/80">AERA Open</a>, and our study of how Louisiana parents search for and choose preschools appeared in <a href="https://doi.org/10.1016/j.ecresq.2018.01.006" class="text-primary underline underline-offset-2 hover:text-primary/80">Early Childhood Research Quarterly</a>. My <a href="https://doi.org/10.18130/v3-gczg-zn95" class="text-primary underline underline-offset-2 hover:text-primary/80">dissertation</a> extended the work, and the <a href="https://www.semanticscholar.org/author/Preston-Magouirk/82801417" class="text-primary underline underline-offset-2 hover:text-primary/80">full list of my publications</a> is public.
								</p>

							</div>
						</div>
					</div>

					<div class="relative">
						<div
							class="absolute -left-[11px] top-2 h-3 w-3 rounded-full border-2 border-white bg-primary"
						></div>
						<div class="pl-6">
							<h3 class="text-h3 font-semibold text-neutral-900">
								Associate Editor | Peabody Journal of Education
							</h3>
							<p class="mt-1 text-base text-neutral-600">2013 – 2015 | Nashville, TN</p>
							<div class="mt-6 space-y-4 text-base leading-relaxed text-neutral-700">
								<p>
									Managed editorial operations, review pipelines, and production scheduling for one
									of the nation's oldest education policy journals while completing MPP coursework.
								</p>
							</div>
						</div>
					</div>

